            "type": "game",
            "name": "Distant Star: Revenant Fleet",
            "steam_appid": 335830,
            "required_age": 0,
            "is_free": false,
            "detailed_description": "<strong>NOW AVAILABLE ON MAC AND LINUX </strong><br><i>In Distant Star: Revenant Fleet, you take control of the last remaining ships of a near-destroyed A’kari fleet, and must rebuild your forces as you battle through ancient, galactic battlefields towards a final showdown with the Orthani. </i><br><br>Build your fleet of up to 5 ships (from a choice of any combination of 8 classes) and upgrade their weapons and attachments which give you new and improved skills to use in combat.  With hundreds of attachments to choose from, each class has many different possible loadouts.<br><br>Traverse the galaxy one system at a time - each step of the way you will face unique story events, each of which has multiple outcomes that can change with each playthrough.  Choose whether or not you enter combat, flee or try to talk your way out of difficult situations - but don't think the same choice next time round will have the same outcome!<br><br><i>All set within a beautifully designed universe with an eerily atmospheric soundtrack - Distant Star: Revenant Fleet is a game you'll be playing again and again...</i>",
            "about_the_game": "<strong>NOW AVAILABLE ON MAC AND LINUX </strong><br><i>In Distant Star: Revenant Fleet, you take control of the last remaining ships of a near-destroyed A’kari fleet, and must rebuild your forces as you battle through ancient, galactic battlefields towards a final showdown with the Orthani. </i><br><br>Build your fleet of up to 5 ships (from a choice of any combination of 8 classes) and upgrade their weapons and attachments which give you new and improved skills to use in combat.  With hundreds of attachments to choose from, each class has many different possible loadouts.<br><br>Traverse the galaxy one system at a time - each step of the way you will face unique story events, each of which has multiple outcomes that can change with each playthrough.  Choose whether or not you enter combat, flee or try to talk your way out of difficult situations - but don't think the same choice next time round will have the same outcome!<br><br><i>All set within a beautifully designed universe with an eerily atmospheric soundtrack - Distant Star: Revenant Fleet is a game you'll be playing again and again...</i>",
            "short_description": "BAFTA award winning fleet-based RTS meets rogue-lite. In Distant Star: Revenant Fleet, build your fleet of up to 5 ships from a choice of 8 classes and traverse a randomly generated galaxy to defeat the Erebus Platform. NOW AVAILABLE ON MAC AND LINUX",
            "supported_languages": "Inglês<strong>*</strong><br><strong>*</strong>idiomas com suporte total de áudio",
            "reviews": {
                "query_summary": {
                    "num_reviews": 1,
                    "review_score": 5,
                    "review_score_desc": "Mixed",
                    "total_positive": 156,
                    "total_negative": 84,
                    "total_reviews": 240
                },
                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "17262920",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198005169152",
                            "num_reviews": 47,
                            "playtime_forever": 347,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 337,
                            "last_played": 1438365774
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": " hm, most of those negative reviews seem to be outdated because the game really feels different to what they claim.\n\nOverall the game is very similar to FTL, you pass through several sectors to reach the final boss fight, every sector has multiple systems, where you can fight, repair, do quests, buy stuff,.... and each jump consumes fuel.\nInstead of managing your crew during a fight you control your fleet (up to 5 ships) from a top down perspective. -Squad-based RTS style.\nBut be warned, the game is a lot slower paced, which makes it more of a RTS game with some light rogue-like elements rather than a rogue-like with RTS elements (if that makes any sense).\n\nOther reviews claimed that the battles are needlessly dragged out but I can't confirm that, they take a few minutes at best and depending on your fleet composition offer a reasonable amount of tactical depth. \nI've also read a lot of complaints about the harsh difficulty. I played on normal and didn't die until I reached the final boss level. (a bit too easy) It felt pretty consistent through each sector until the very last room, where it really spiked and I was killed before I could even reach the boss (a bit too difficult) but the devs seem to be very active so I hope they will have a second look at this.\n\nBut all in all, I really enjoyed it.\n",
                        "timestamp_created": 1438076314,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1438076314,
                        "voted_up": true,
                        "votes_up": 93,
                        "votes_funny": 1,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.8509401679039001,
                        "comment_count": 4,
                        "steam_purchase": true,
                        "received_for_free": false,
                        "written_during_early_access": false,
                        "developer_response": "Hi MayhemMike, thanks for your review!\n\nYes, quite a few of the reviews are from earlier in the year and many of the issues raised have been addressed in subsequent patches.  Our Dev Roadmap has an idea of the dates of those patches to compare with review dates:  http://www.blazinggriffin.com/games/distant-star-revenant-fleet/development-roadmap/\n\nThere has been some feedback from the most recent patch about the difficulty of the final battle and this is something the team are having a look at.\n\nGlad you're enjoying the game and if you have any questions about it, please ask. :)",
                        "timestamp_dev_responded": 1438078651,
                        "primarily_steam_deck": false,
                        "refunded": false
                    }
                ],
